==Trivia==
*Originally, when ''[[RuneScape 2]]'' was released, the lair was mapped by the [[Temple of Ikov (dungeon)|Temple of Ikov]]. It was later changed due to [[safespot|safespotting]].{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/jagexash/status/497400311284518912|date=7 August 2014|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/107893|archivedate=24 September 2018|quote=When RuneScape 2 came out, the KBD lair was mapped by the Temple of Ikov. It changed due to safe-spotting.}} Players who were in the icy area of the Temple of Ikov dungeon could see some of the old KBD lair's tiles on their minimap, and even hear the lava bubbling if they stood close enough to the western wall. Like the current lair, the KBD was located in the centre accompanied with an [[uncut sapphire]] and scattered [[coins|coin]] [[Item spawn|spawns]]. The teleport [[lever]] was located one tile west of the southernmost skeleton. After the current lair was created, the KBD could be seen wandering in the old lair for a while. The lever and item spawns were removed, although the chests and other scenery remained. Years later, the old lair no longer exists at all in-game after an update.
[[File:Old KBD Lair.png|thumb|left|The former KBD Lair, which was previously visible by using the [[oculus orb]].]]
